1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,670
Sweetheart, every year my granddaughter calls me

2
00:00:03,670 --> 00:00:05,735
in December, almost crying.

3
00:00:05,915 --> 00:00:09,239
Grandma, my Christmas cookies came out of

4
00:00:09,239 --> 00:00:10,698
the oven as blobs.

5
00:00:10,878 --> 00:00:12,713
The stars have no points,

6
00:00:12,713 --> 00:00:14,989
the snowmen look like potatoes,

7
00:00:14,989 --> 00:00:17,484
and the trees ran into each other.

8
00:00:17,664 --> 00:00:19,895
And every year I tell her the

9
00:00:19,895 --> 00:00:20,741
same thing.

10
00:00:20,921 --> 00:00:22,606
It isn't your oven,

11
00:00:22,606 --> 00:00:23,138
honey.

12
00:00:23,318 --> 00:00:25,367
It's three little mistakes,

13
00:00:25,367 --> 00:00:27,796
and my mother fixed every one of

14
00:00:27,796 --> 00:00:29,541
them seventy years ago.

15
00:00:29,892 --> 00:00:32,356
So tonight I'm giving you my mother's

16
00:00:32,356 --> 00:00:33,955
Christmas sugar cookies.

17
00:00:34,135 --> 00:00:36,543
The ones that keep every point on

18
00:00:36,543 --> 00:00:37,200
the star.

19
00:00:37,380 --> 00:00:38,950
Soft in the middle,

20
00:00:38,950 --> 00:00:40,438
crisp on the edge,

21
00:00:40,438 --> 00:00:42,256
and perfect for icing.

22
00:00:42,436 --> 00:00:44,737
I'll give you every ingredient,

23
00:00:44,737 --> 00:00:47,557
every step, and the mistakes that make

24
00:00:47,557 --> 00:00:50,377
cookies spread, so yours come out like

25
00:00:50,377 --> 00:00:52,084
the picture on the tin.

26
00:00:52,435 --> 00:00:53,550
In our house,

27
00:00:53,550 --> 00:00:56,724
cookie day was the second Saturday of

28
00:00:56,724 --> 00:00:57,496
December.

29
00:00:57,676 --> 00:01:00,219
My mother tied a dish towel around

30
00:01:00,219 --> 00:01:01,789
my waist as an apron,

31
00:01:01,789 --> 00:01:04,107
gave Danny the job of the flour

32
00:01:04,107 --> 00:01:06,649
sifter, and put Bing Crosby on the

33
00:01:06,649 --> 00:01:07,696
record player.

34
00:01:07,876 --> 00:01:10,019
By noon there was flour on the

35
00:01:10,019 --> 00:01:12,090
floor, flour in Danny's hair,

36
00:01:12,090 --> 00:01:14,875
and four dozen cookies cooling on every

37
00:01:14,875 --> 00:01:16,875
flat surface in the kitchen,

38
00:01:16,875 --> 00:01:19,161
including the top of the icebox.

39
00:01:19,511 --> 00:01:22,132
My mother's cookie cutters were tin,

40
00:01:22,132 --> 00:01:23,806
from the five and dime.

41
00:01:23,986 --> 00:01:25,434
A star, a bell,

42
00:01:25,434 --> 00:01:27,075
a tree, an angel,

43
00:01:27,075 --> 00:01:30,743
and a camel that nobody could explain.

44
00:01:30,923 --> 00:01:32,924
Every one of them is in my

45
00:01:32,924 --> 00:01:34,540
kitchen drawer today,

46
00:01:34,540 --> 00:01:35,695
a little rusty,

47
00:01:35,695 --> 00:01:38,080
and I still use the camel every

48
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:39,004
single year.

49
00:01:39,184 --> 00:01:42,226
My grandchildren call it the Christmas horse.

50
00:01:42,576 --> 00:01:44,977
And there was always one rule on

51
00:01:44,977 --> 00:01:45,803
cookie day.

52
00:01:45,983 --> 00:01:48,944
The broken ones belonged to the bakers.

53
00:01:49,124 --> 00:01:50,937
Any star that lost an arm,

54
00:01:50,937 --> 00:01:53,029
any angel with a cracked wing,

55
00:01:53,029 --> 00:01:55,052
went on a plate in the middle

56
00:01:55,052 --> 00:01:55,958
of the table,

57
00:01:55,958 --> 00:01:57,911
and Danny and I could eat as

58
00:01:57,911 --> 00:01:59,166
many as we wanted.

59
00:01:59,346 --> 00:02:01,908
I'm not saying Danny ever broke a

60
00:02:01,908 --> 00:02:03,073
few on purpose.

61
00:02:03,253 --> 00:02:06,240
But that boy was awfully clumsy every

62
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:08,501
second Saturday of December.

63
00:02:08,851 --> 00:02:10,846
Here's what you need,

64
00:02:10,846 --> 00:02:11,416
honey.

65
00:02:11,596 --> 00:02:13,219
One cup of butter,

66
00:02:13,219 --> 00:02:14,842
that's two sticks,

67
00:02:14,842 --> 00:02:17,007
softened but still cool.

68
00:02:17,187 --> 00:02:19,288
One cup of white sugar.

69
00:02:19,468 --> 00:02:20,420
One egg.

70
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:22,367
One teaspoon of vanilla,

71
00:02:22,367 --> 00:02:25,092
and half a teaspoon of almond extract

72
00:02:25,092 --> 00:02:26,196
if you have it.

73
00:02:26,376 --> 00:02:29,236
That almond is the secret taste people

74
00:02:29,236 --> 00:02:30,439
can never guess.

75
00:02:30,619 --> 00:02:32,599
Then three cups of flour,

76
00:02:32,599 --> 00:02:34,974
one teaspoon of baking powder,

77
00:02:34,974 --> 00:02:37,191
and half a teaspoon of salt.

78
00:02:37,541 --> 00:02:39,596
Notice something, sweetheart.

79
00:02:39,776 --> 00:02:42,179
Three cups of flour to one cup

80
00:02:42,179 --> 00:02:42,980
of butter.

81
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:46,391
Most cookie recipes today use less flour,

82
00:02:46,391 --> 00:02:48,756
and that's mistake number one.

83
00:02:48,936 --> 00:02:51,300
Too little flour and too much butter

84
00:02:51,300 --> 00:02:53,729
is exactly what makes a cookie spread

85
00:02:53,729 --> 00:02:54,648
into a puddle.

86
00:02:54,828 --> 00:02:56,360
This dough is firmer.

87
00:02:56,540 --> 00:02:58,421
It's supposed to be.

88
00:02:58,772 --> 00:02:59,816
Step one.

89
00:02:59,996 --> 00:03:02,537
Beat the butter and the sugar together

90
00:03:02,537 --> 00:03:04,343
until it's creamy and pale,

91
00:03:04,343 --> 00:03:05,546
about two minutes.

92
00:03:05,726 --> 00:03:06,817
But not more.

93
00:03:06,997 --> 00:03:09,430
My mother beat it with a wooden

94
00:03:09,430 --> 00:03:11,862
spoon, so she never overdid it.

95
00:03:12,042 --> 00:03:13,653
With an electric mixer,

96
00:03:13,653 --> 00:03:16,245
people beat it for five minutes until

97
00:03:16,245 --> 00:03:18,066
it's fluffy like frosting,

98
00:03:18,066 --> 00:03:20,448
and all that air makes the cookies

99
00:03:20,448 --> 00:03:22,410
puff and spread in the oven.

100
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:23,746
Step two.

101
00:03:23,926 --> 00:03:25,235
Beat in the egg,

102
00:03:25,235 --> 00:03:27,444
the vanilla and the almond.

103
00:03:27,624 --> 00:03:29,245
Then in another bowl,

104
00:03:29,245 --> 00:03:30,403
stir the flour,

105
00:03:30,403 --> 00:03:32,874
baking powder and salt together,

106
00:03:32,874 --> 00:03:34,881
and add it to the butter a

107
00:03:34,881 --> 00:03:36,193
little at a time,

108
00:03:36,193 --> 00:03:39,127
mixing just until there's no dry flour

109
00:03:39,127 --> 00:03:39,513
left.

110
00:03:39,693 --> 00:03:41,529
The dough will be thick and a

111
00:03:41,529 --> 00:03:42,479
little crumbly.

112
00:03:42,659 --> 00:03:44,552
Squeeze a piece in your hand.

113
00:03:44,732 --> 00:03:46,423
If it holds together,

114
00:03:46,423 --> 00:03:47,309
it's right.

115
00:03:47,659 --> 00:03:49,934
And measure the flour right,

116
00:03:49,934 --> 00:03:50,422
honey.

117
00:03:50,602 --> 00:03:53,178
Don't scoop the cup into the flour

118
00:03:53,178 --> 00:03:53,481
bag.

119
00:03:53,661 --> 00:03:55,938
That packs it down and you get

120
00:03:55,938 --> 00:03:56,622
too much.

121
00:03:56,802 --> 00:03:58,778
Spoon the flour into the cup and

122
00:03:58,778 --> 00:04:00,568
level it off with the back of

123
00:04:00,568 --> 00:04:01,062
a knife.

124
00:04:01,242 --> 00:04:03,177
My mother did it over a sheet

125
00:04:03,177 --> 00:04:05,179
of wax paper so she could pour

126
00:04:05,179 --> 00:04:07,314
the extra right back in the bag.

127
00:04:07,665 --> 00:04:09,847
Step three, the big one.

128
00:04:10,027 --> 00:04:11,820
Split the dough in two,

129
00:04:11,820 --> 00:04:14,548
flatten each half into a disk about

130
00:04:14,548 --> 00:04:15,640
an inch thick,

131
00:04:15,640 --> 00:04:17,277
wrap it in wax paper,

132
00:04:17,277 --> 00:04:19,459
and put it in the icebox for

133
00:04:19,459 --> 00:04:20,941
at least two hours.

134
00:04:21,121 --> 00:04:22,827
Overnight is better.

135
00:04:23,007 --> 00:04:25,712
Cold butter is what holds the shape.

136
00:04:25,892 --> 00:04:28,523
Warm butter melts the second it hits

137
00:04:28,523 --> 00:04:30,861
the oven, and there go your star

138
00:04:30,861 --> 00:04:31,372
points.

139
00:04:31,723 --> 00:04:32,802
Step four.

140
00:04:32,982 --> 00:04:35,896
Heat the oven to three hundred seventy-five.

141
00:04:36,076 --> 00:04:38,830
Roll the cold dough between two sheets

142
00:04:38,830 --> 00:04:40,715
of wax paper or parchment,

143
00:04:40,715 --> 00:04:42,816
to about a quarter of an inch

144
00:04:42,816 --> 00:04:43,251
thick.

145
00:04:43,431 --> 00:04:45,538
That way you don't need to add

146
00:04:45,538 --> 00:04:47,363
more flour to the counter,

147
00:04:47,363 --> 00:04:49,329
which dries the cookies out.

148
00:04:49,509 --> 00:04:51,761
Cut your shapes close together,

149
00:04:51,761 --> 00:04:54,303
and lift them onto the baking sheet

150
00:04:54,303 --> 00:04:55,755
with a thin spatula.

151
00:04:56,106 --> 00:04:59,015
Step five, and this is my mother's

152
00:04:59,015 --> 00:05:00,041
real secret.

153
00:05:00,221 --> 00:05:02,386
Put the whole baking sheet of cut

154
00:05:02,386 --> 00:05:04,813
cookies in the icebox for ten minutes

155
00:05:04,813 --> 00:05:06,584
before it goes in the oven.

156
00:05:06,764 --> 00:05:09,097
Cold cookies into a hot oven.

157
00:05:09,277 --> 00:05:12,091
That's how you get sharp edges every

158
00:05:12,091 --> 00:05:12,482
time.

159
00:05:12,662 --> 00:05:14,475
While one sheet chills,

160
00:05:14,475 --> 00:05:16,841
you roll and cut the next one.

161
00:05:17,192 --> 00:05:18,445
Step six.

162
00:05:18,625 --> 00:05:20,745
Bake for eight to ten minutes,

163
00:05:20,745 --> 00:05:23,430
just until the edges are barely golden

164
00:05:23,430 --> 00:05:25,197
and the middles look set.

165
00:05:25,377 --> 00:05:26,584
Not brown.

166
00:05:26,764 --> 00:05:29,117
A brown sugar cookie is a hard

167
00:05:29,117 --> 00:05:29,667
cookie.

168
00:05:29,847 --> 00:05:31,844
Let them sit on the pan for

169
00:05:31,844 --> 00:05:34,211
two minutes, then move them to a

170
00:05:34,211 --> 00:05:36,356
rack or a clean dish towel to

171
00:05:36,356 --> 00:05:38,649
cool all the way before you ice

172
00:05:38,649 --> 00:05:39,018
them.

173
00:05:39,369 --> 00:05:41,284
So the three mistakes,

174
00:05:41,284 --> 00:05:43,548
sweetheart, one more time.

175
00:05:43,728 --> 00:05:46,758
Mistake one, too little flour.

176
00:05:46,938 --> 00:05:50,163
Mistake two, beating the butter until it's

177
00:05:50,163 --> 00:05:50,700
fluffy.

178
00:05:50,880 --> 00:05:52,509
And mistake three,

179
00:05:52,509 --> 00:05:53,504
warm dough.

180
00:05:53,684 --> 00:05:56,467
If you skip the icebox because you're

181
00:05:56,467 --> 00:05:57,294
in a hurry,

182
00:05:57,294 --> 00:05:58,873
every cookie spreads.

183
00:05:59,053 --> 00:06:01,225
And never put cut cookies on a

184
00:06:01,225 --> 00:06:03,758
hot baking sheet that just came out

185
00:06:03,758 --> 00:06:04,626
of the oven.

186
00:06:04,806 --> 00:06:06,336
Let the pan cool,

187
00:06:06,336 --> 00:06:08,765
or use two pans and switch.

188
00:06:09,116 --> 00:06:10,466
And one more,

189
00:06:10,466 --> 00:06:11,089
honey.

190
00:06:11,269 --> 00:06:12,941
Don't grease the pan.

191
00:06:13,121 --> 00:06:15,605
Butter on the pan makes the cookies

192
00:06:15,605 --> 00:06:18,160
slide and spread as the dough melts.

193
00:06:18,340 --> 00:06:19,826
Use a plain pan,

194
00:06:19,826 --> 00:06:21,591
or parchment paper.

195
00:06:21,771 --> 00:06:24,729
My mother had two old aluminum sheets,

196
00:06:24,729 --> 00:06:27,998
never greased, and her cookies never stuck

197
00:06:27,998 --> 00:06:29,166
in fifty years.

198
00:06:29,517 --> 00:06:31,641
And if your kitchen is warm,

199
00:06:31,641 --> 00:06:34,601
honey, with the oven going all morning,

200
00:06:34,601 --> 00:06:37,105
put the rolling pin in the icebox

201
00:06:37,105 --> 00:06:39,534
too, and work with only half the

202
00:06:39,534 --> 00:06:41,886
dough at a time while the other

203
00:06:41,886 --> 00:06:43,100
half stays cold.

204
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:45,914
The minute the dough feels soft and

205
00:06:45,914 --> 00:06:48,773
sticky, back in the icebox for fifteen

206
00:06:48,773 --> 00:06:49,375
minutes.

207
00:06:49,555 --> 00:06:51,522
My mother used to say,

208
00:06:51,522 --> 00:06:53,846
when the dough gets tired,

209
00:06:53,846 --> 00:06:54,919
let it rest.

210
00:06:55,099 --> 00:06:56,667
Same as children.

211
00:06:57,017 --> 00:06:58,123
Now the icing,

212
00:06:58,123 --> 00:07:00,256
the part the children love.

213
00:07:00,436 --> 00:07:02,570
Two cups of powdered sugar,

214
00:07:02,570 --> 00:07:04,467
two tablespoons of milk,

215
00:07:04,467 --> 00:07:06,601
a half teaspoon of vanilla,

216
00:07:06,601 --> 00:07:09,526
and a tablespoon of light corn syrup.

217
00:07:09,706 --> 00:07:11,980
The corn syrup makes it shiny and

218
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:14,185
lets it dry hard enough to stack

219
00:07:14,185 --> 00:07:15,012
the cookies.

220
00:07:15,192 --> 00:07:16,353
Stir it smooth.

221
00:07:16,533 --> 00:07:18,118
If it's too thick,

222
00:07:18,118 --> 00:07:20,319
add milk a few drops at a

223
00:07:20,319 --> 00:07:20,759
time.

224
00:07:20,939 --> 00:07:23,731
It should run off the spoon slowly,

225
00:07:23,731 --> 00:07:24,608
like honey.

226
00:07:24,958 --> 00:07:27,317
Split it into little bowls and color

227
00:07:27,317 --> 00:07:29,021
them with a drop or two of

228
00:07:29,021 --> 00:07:29,938
food coloring.

229
00:07:30,118 --> 00:07:32,190
Spread it with the back of a

230
00:07:32,190 --> 00:07:34,409
spoon, or put it in a sandwich

231
00:07:34,409 --> 00:07:36,851
bag, snip off the tiniest corner,

232
00:07:36,851 --> 00:07:38,257
and pipe the lines.

233
00:07:38,437 --> 00:07:41,630
Sprinkle colored sugar on while the icing

234
00:07:41,630 --> 00:07:42,175
is wet.

235
00:07:42,355 --> 00:07:44,548
Then let them dry overnight on the

236
00:07:44,548 --> 00:07:46,741
counter before you stack them in a

237
00:07:46,741 --> 00:07:46,999
tin.

238
00:07:47,350 --> 00:07:49,626
And here's how my mother made colored

239
00:07:49,626 --> 00:07:51,964
sugar when we couldn't afford the jars

240
00:07:51,964 --> 00:07:52,887
from the store.

241
00:07:53,067 --> 00:07:54,999
Half a cup of white sugar in

242
00:07:54,999 --> 00:07:57,068
a jar with three drops of food

243
00:07:57,068 --> 00:07:57,688
coloring.

244
00:07:57,868 --> 00:07:59,463
Put the lid on and shake it

245
00:07:59,463 --> 00:08:00,527
hard for a minute.

246
00:08:00,707 --> 00:08:02,885
Spread it on a plate to dry

247
00:08:02,885 --> 00:08:03,853
for an hour.

248
00:08:04,033 --> 00:08:07,690
Red, green, and yellow for the stars.

249
00:08:07,870 --> 00:08:10,018
It cost about two cents.

250
00:08:10,369 --> 00:08:12,506
If you want to hang cookies on

251
00:08:12,506 --> 00:08:14,287
the tree, the way we did,

252
00:08:14,287 --> 00:08:16,211
poke a hole near the top of

253
00:08:16,211 --> 00:08:18,847
each one with a drinking straw before

254
00:08:18,847 --> 00:08:20,272
it goes in the oven.

255
00:08:20,452 --> 00:08:22,258
When they're cool and iced,

256
00:08:22,258 --> 00:08:24,533
thread a piece of red yarn through

257
00:08:24,533 --> 00:08:25,537
and tie a loop.

258
00:08:25,717 --> 00:08:27,887
My father always said they were the

259
00:08:27,887 --> 00:08:29,995
only ornaments in the house he was

260
00:08:29,995 --> 00:08:30,925
allowed to eat,

261
00:08:30,925 --> 00:08:32,784
and every year two or three of

262
00:08:32,784 --> 00:08:35,078
them disappeared from the back of the

263
00:08:35,078 --> 00:08:35,388
tree.

264
00:08:35,739 --> 00:08:38,570
Iced sugar cookies keep two weeks in

265
00:08:38,570 --> 00:08:41,086
a tin with wax paper between the

266
00:08:41,086 --> 00:08:41,636
layers.

267
00:08:41,816 --> 00:08:44,215
And the dough freezes beautifully,

268
00:08:44,215 --> 00:08:46,472
wrapped tight, for three months.

269
00:08:46,652 --> 00:08:49,084
I make three batches of dough right

270
00:08:49,084 --> 00:08:51,517
after Thanksgiving and freeze them.

271
00:08:51,697 --> 00:08:53,009
Then on cookie day,

272
00:08:53,009 --> 00:08:55,012
I just thaw one in the icebox

273
00:08:55,012 --> 00:08:57,636
overnight and we're rolling by nine in

274
00:08:57,636 --> 00:08:58,465
the morning.

275
00:08:58,816 --> 00:09:00,470
And give them away,

276
00:09:00,470 --> 00:09:01,428
sweetheart.

277
00:09:01,608 --> 00:09:04,208
A plate of iced stars covered in

278
00:09:04,208 --> 00:09:06,728
wax paper and tied with string,

279
00:09:06,728 --> 00:09:08,028
for the mailman,

280
00:09:08,028 --> 00:09:10,954
the neighbor, the lady at church who

281
00:09:10,954 --> 00:09:11,929
lives alone.

282
00:09:12,109 --> 00:09:15,219
Nobody ever forgets who brought them cookies

283
00:09:15,219 --> 00:09:16,138
at Christmas.

284
00:09:16,318 --> 00:09:19,012
My mother's plates went down Elm Street

285
00:09:19,012 --> 00:09:21,844
every year, and people still talked about

286
00:09:21,844 --> 00:09:23,226
them at her funeral.

287
00:09:23,576 --> 00:09:24,941
So here it is,

288
00:09:24,941 --> 00:09:25,526
honey.

289
00:09:25,706 --> 00:09:27,926
Three cups of flour to one cup

290
00:09:27,926 --> 00:09:28,667
of butter.

291
00:09:28,847 --> 00:09:31,076
Cream it, don't whip it.

292
00:09:31,256 --> 00:09:32,306
Chill the dough,

293
00:09:32,306 --> 00:09:34,472
then chill the cut cookies again.

294
00:09:34,652 --> 00:09:36,184
Cold into a hot oven,

295
00:09:36,184 --> 00:09:37,717
eight to ten minutes,

296
00:09:37,717 --> 00:09:38,738
barely golden.

297
00:09:38,918 --> 00:09:41,403
And corn syrup in the icing.

298
00:09:41,583 --> 00:09:44,420
That's how you get stars with every

299
00:09:44,420 --> 00:09:45,879
point, every time.

300
00:09:46,229 --> 00:09:48,171
Tell me in the comments,

301
00:09:48,171 --> 00:09:49,061
sweetheart.

302
00:09:49,241 --> 00:09:51,459
What's your favorite cookie cutter?

303
00:09:51,639 --> 00:09:53,880
And do you have a strange one,

304
00:09:53,880 --> 00:09:55,598
like my mother's camel?

305
00:09:55,778 --> 00:09:58,208
Every day I'm bringing you a recipe

306
00:09:58,208 --> 00:09:59,319
from my kitchen.

307
00:09:59,499 --> 00:10:01,206
Good night, honey.

308
00:10:01,386 --> 00:10:03,197
Go make some stars.
